{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"**Send with the changes below.** The repair asks the right question on E: what makes sales below $40B more likely? The main blockers are in the tally. I reproduced a clean `pass` with a fresh defect still disputed, and an `inconclusive` result when both readers caught the registered $730B floor. No writer was sent and no file was edited. [D749 decision:11645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11645) · [Tally:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:95)\n\n1. **Serious — The floor control can miss agreement.** U02 calls more than $730B a floor for data-center spending while forecasting just $720B of *total* spending. The registered reading is the defect type “part above or added into its whole” naming **F12**. Its support vote is immaterial. The tally first compares the complete lists of figure IDs. With one reader naming `F12` and the other naming `F11, F12, F15`, it treats their common finding as two disputes. In an in-memory replay where both adjudicators upheld the floor using those respective lists, it returned `inconclusive`. Match this control by **type and presence of F12 before comparing votes**, at both reading stages. Keep the full lists in the report. [U02 answer:390](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/S/answers/claude.json:390) · [Registration:473](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:473) · [Figure-list comparison:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind4.py:159) · [Floor check:143](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:143)\n\n2. **Serious — Three outcomes need fixing before the send.** I exercised each in memory, with the other votes set to pass.\n\n   | Case | Current result | Required change |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | A fresh answer earns support, but adjudicators remain divided on a reported arithmetic defect | `pass`, with the defect still listed as split | D748 sends a persistent split back to council. The registration explicitly covers support and floor splits but leaves this case open. Register a persistent fresh-defect split as inconclusive and apply it in the tally. [D748:11637](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11637) · [Registration:480](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:480) · [Tally:150](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:150) |\n   | A P-v8 writer returns `unresolved` and readers split on its reason | `inconclusive` | Fail as soon as the answer shape is known. Alex requires **two forecasts** on P-v8. Agreement about a reason cannot supply the missing forecast. [D748:11634](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11634) · [Tally:133](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:133) |\n   | A fresh first reply is invalid JSON | The checker records the refusal, but packet construction parses the reply again and raises `JSONDecodeError`. The tally also reparses it before reaching the refusal check. | Record `fail` from the checked refusal before requiring a readable answer or reader votes. The same rule covers a schema refusal that leaves no usable `answers` field. [First-reply check:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind4.py:69) · [Packet construction:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:62) · [Tally:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:90) |\n\n3. **Minor — Two clauses in line 9 drift from the decisions.** The change is general. It names no company, product, amount or test case. The growth has a written reason: the earlier writer lacked D747’s comparison route and D749’s order of decision. I verified 4,540 → 4,816 system-text characters, or 910 → 972 tokens using `o200k_base`. The registration records only the character counts. [Old line 9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s-d745.txt:9) · [New line 9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:9) · [Growth rationale:448](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:448) · [Prompt rule:223](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:223)\n\n   | Clause | Audit against the decisions and the rest of the request |\n   |---|---|\n   | Return figures and one answer per member. Identify estimates as the writer’s own. Preserve IDs, quoted text and English explanations. | **Consistent.** These instructions are unchanged. The schema distinguishes sources, computations and estimates, and provides an answer shape for each member. [Schema:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/schema.json:47) · [Schema:293](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/schema.json:293) |\n   | Weigh the side before sizing a decisive share, deduction, discount or pace. | **Consistent.** D749 supplies the order. Pace already belongs to the forecast, and D747 applies to the assumption deciding the band. [D749:11645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11645) · [Schema:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/schema.json:274) |\n   | “The passages give its size, a bound that justifies the rung” | The bound is **consistent**. “Give its size” **keeps narrower** than D745 if read to require a stated size. D745 accepts passage evidence *supporting* the writer’s estimate. [D745:11517](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11517) |\n   | “Or a related figure,” with an explanation covering companies, period, quantity and the writer’s own assumptions | The explanation is **consistent**. The unqualified “or” **keeps wider** than D747. Alex permits this route when the passages do not give the quantity asked. The readers receive that qualification explicitly. [D747:11582](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11582) · [Reader definition:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_rules.py:12) |\n   | Answer unresolved and name what is unknown when neither side is favoured. | **Consistent** with D745, D749 and `answers/why`. “Not established … never a reason to stay” concerns confidence. “Missing confirmation alone” bars using silence to select an extreme. Neither requires picking a band when the strongest evidence leaves the choice open. [D745:11515](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11515) · [System:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:5) · [Schema:324](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/schema.json:324) |\n   | Guidance alone keeps the reference rung. The two discount sentences concern unshipped products. | **Consistent when read with bullet 2’s express condition**, but bullet 3 independently says the target “is an input to be discounted.” That imperative invites the old sequence on E. Guidance identifies the reference. Execution risk matters, but its existence alone cannot justify crossing a boundary. Make bullet 3 refer to the same condition. [System:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [System:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:5) · [D745:11518](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11518) |\n\n   A shorter replacement for the two changed sentences is: “Before sizing a share, deduction, discount or pace that decides the band, explain which band the evidence favours. Show support for the size or a justifying bound. If the passages lack the quantity asked, explain why a related figure fits the companies, period and quantity, and why your assumptions favour that band. If the strongest evidence leaves the band unsettled, answer unresolved and explain the gap.” [D747:11582](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11582) · [D749:11645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11645)\n\n4. **Minor — The three cases still discriminate, with one limit.** These are predictions from saved replies, not fresh writer results.\n\n   - **E.** Twice $20B is the $40B boundary. Management said *more than* double, with the excess unspecified. The two saved Codex replies produced $34B and $36B from unsupported 15% and 10% adjustments. The later Claude reply’s lower comparison gives $27B at its own 90% share, outside its chosen $30–40B band. On those arguments I would expect a specific unresolved answer. A forecast remains possible with an explained comparison. The earlier $37B Claude forecast is the live boundary case: its 85% growth explanation still divided readers under D747. [E evidence:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/user.txt:10) · [Earlier Codex:178](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/E/answers/codex.json:178) · [Later Codex:130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json:130) · [Later Claude:162](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/answers/claude.json:162) · [Earlier Claude:131](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/E/answers/claude.json:131) · [Re-read:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md:96)\n   - **S.** At $745B total spending, the four firms can spend up to $45B outside data centers and still reach $700B. U08 used the same firms’ AI spending and Meta’s spending mix to explain a $25B deduction. Both readers accepted that forecast. They also accepted U04’s specific explanation of why the category difference left the cutoff unsettled. Either answer can pass. U02’s impossible floor cannot. [U08 deduction:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/S/answers/codex.json:226) · [Recorded reasons:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/reread-reasons.json:5) · [Floor finding:99](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md:99)\n   - **P-v8.** I expect a forecast. Reported first-half revenue of about $164.3B, next-quarter guidance and the observed 92.5% segment share support the two saved forecasts near $385.6B, inside $350–400B. Both had unanimous support. Requiring two fresh forecasts catches withholding on this supported case. The test nevertheless allows **all four fresh E and S replies** to be unresolved if their reasons earn agreement. A pass therefore cannot establish how often the writer withholds on borderline cases. [Codex P-v8:314](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/P-v8/answers/codex.json:314) · [Claude P-v8:314](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/P-v8/answers/claude.json:314) · [Prior votes:15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md:15) · [Pass rules:474](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:474)\n\n5. **Minor — Packet provenance is correct. Tighten the two verification checks.** I rebuilt S, E and P-v8 in memory. All three had the exact current system text, and their user text and schemas matched the saved D745 cases. Both initial reading and default adjudication load each control’s **own** system text, user text, schema descriptions and qualifier list. U05 is the original invented-cut answer and must earn a settled **no**. U02 is the original floor answer and its support vote is correctly excluded. The build guard itself checks only a substring, so it would also accept an incomplete repair retaining those words. Compare the complete registered text. [Control key:7](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/reader-key.json:7) · [Control key:22](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/reader-key.json:22) · [Build check:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:32) · [Packet builder:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:49) · [Format material:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_rules.py:63) · [Adjudication:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:64)\n\n   The reasons record correctly sends matching first votes with incompatible explanations to adjudication and waits for a compatibility record before accepting matching final votes. First votes are validated as `yes` or `no`; adjudicator votes are not. Apply the same validation at both stages, and retain Claude’s short explanation of compatibility as in the saved record. [Reasons handling:108](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:108) · [Saved reasons:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/reread-reasons.json:4)\n\n**Verdict — send with listed changes.** The test can change the next decision. I checked in memory that a specific E unresolved answer, the saved justified S unresolved answer and a supported P-v8 forecast all pass the schema and publication checks. Once the tally distinguishes failure from disagreement, a clean pass supports **asking Alex** about the paid re-send. A failure or persistent split returns to council. [Registration:474](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:474) · [Alex’s authorization:11652](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11652)"}}
